    "profile_text": {
        "body": "NVIDIA is a public company founded in 1993 and headquartered in Santa Clara, California. Its website describes the NVIDIA Nemotron family as multimodal, open AI models built for long-running, self-evolving agents, with transparent training data and support for NVIDIA RTX PRO and NVIDIA DGX Spark. The company says Nemotron models are openly available and integrated across the AI ecosystem, and that the NVIDIA Open Model License permits use, modification, distribution, and commercial deployment without crediting NVIDIA.\n\nThe company's AI products include NVIDIA Nemotron, an enterprise LLM family with synthetic data generation and GPU-optimized self-hosted options, and NVIDIA NIM, inference microservices for deploying foundation models with enterprise GPU optimization and self-hosted options. The site states that Nemotron models are available as NVIDIA NIM microservices, which require an NVIDIA AI Enterprise license, and that NVIDIA provides tools such as NVIDIA Dynamo, TensorRT-LLM, and NIM to run Nemotron models at scale. It also mentions NVIDIA NeMo for custom agentic AI and NVIDIA Blueprints for reference workflows.\n\nFor the fiscal period ended January 25, 2026, NVIDIA reported revenue of $215,938,000,000 in a 10-K filing. The company has SEC CIK 0001045810 and trades under ticker NVDA. Its legal exposure includes 281 entries in California, with no listed cases.",
